## 2. UNDERSTAND THE IDENTITY OF ICYOS

ICYOS is an ICY ecosystem application launcher.

It is NOT a new operating system.

It is NOT a virtual machine.

It is NOT an application container that embeds other applications inside its own interface.

It is NOT a website that merely displays decorative app icons.

ICYOS is an installable, cross-device launcher that organizes and launches supported ICY applications and compatible third-party applications.

The user's original operating system remains responsible for running the applications.

For example:

- A user opens ICYOS on a laptop.
- The user sees the ICY application library.
- The user taps ICY Pad.
- ICYOS requests that ICY Pad open as a separate application in the host operating system.
- ICY Pad operates independently of the ICYOS launcher.
- When the user returns to ICYOS, the launcher remains available.

Follow the same principle for mobile phones, tablets, and other supported devices.

Where an actual external application cannot be launched because of browser, operating-system, installation, or permission restrictions, explain the limitation and provide an appropriate installation, connection, or compatibility flow.

Never claim an external app launched successfully when it did not.

Never pretend that a browser has permissions it does not possess.

Design the code around platform adapters so that native launcher functionality can be connected to supported desktop or mobile operating-system APIs when available.

If this project currently runs as a web application, PWA, or browser-based prototype, preserve that working environment and implement all functionality that the environment genuinely supports. Make the architecture ready for native integration without falsely claiming that browser code is a fully privileged native launcher.

