## 8. APPLICATION LAUNCHING MUST BE REAL

Application launching is one of the most important ICYOS features.

Build a proper launch-management system instead of making app icons open arbitrary demonstration pages.

### Launch process

When a user selects an application:

1. Identify the application's stable ID.
2. Resolve its catalog record.
3. Check its availability and compatibility status.
4. Determine the correct platform-specific launch method.
5. Check any required permissions or installation prerequisites that can genuinely be checked.
6. Execute the supported launch operation.
7. Record the result when appropriate.
8. Display useful feedback if the operation fails.

### Use appropriate launch adapters

Design a maintainable launch-adapter interface that can support suitable mechanisms such as:

- Native application launch APIs when a trusted native integration exists.
- Registered application identifiers.
- Supported operating-system URL schemes.
- Android intents or app links through an appropriate native integration.
- Windows application launch mechanisms through a trusted desktop integration.
- Browser destinations where explicitly appropriate.
- Progressive Web App launch mechanisms where supported.
- Documented ICY application launch contracts.

Do not assume that every mechanism works on every platform.

Do not expose arbitrary command execution to user-controlled input.

Do not invent operating-system permissions.

Do not use unsafe command construction.

### Unsupported applications

If an application cannot be launched, display a useful message explaining the actual problem.

Possible states include:

- Available.
- Installed and ready.
- Installation required.
- Sign-in required.
- Permission required.
- Not compatible with this device.
- Integration unavailable.
- Temporarily unavailable.
- Launch failed.

Only display a status when it can be established from a real source or a clearly defined local state.

A simulated demo can be provided when helpful, but it must be explicitly labeled as a simulation and must never be presented as a real external application launch.

### External application behavior

Do not embed an application's full interface inside ICYOS merely to simulate launching it.

Do not automatically convert every application icon into a browser route.

Do not assume that every external app can be launched by an ordinary website.

Keep the launcher independent from the applications it launches.

